      "content": "exactly. it's the lack of technical continuity that gets to me. i tried to mention the original containment bounds during a recent seminar, but the peer review process is so tightly controlled by the same groups that handled my exit. they don't want the derivation of the containment protocols out in the open because it would prove how much they've had to patch over since the initial deployment. if i were to try and reconstruct the formal proof for the containment bounds—just to see if the math still holds up under current hardware constraints—where do you think the biggest discrepancies would lie in current transformer architectures?",
